  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "Classify the target as faithful-stronger. It supplies the selected spectral Riemann solution for every source matrix and state pair, while additionally certifying a particular representative construction on all real times. This decision follows from the declarations and source, not agreement between judges.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed pages 1 and 3 specify the constant real system and complete real eigenvector family. Printed pages 5–6 assert spectral Riemann solvability. The target and D001–D006 retain these objects and add explicit global rectangle conservation and universally parameterized interface values."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The requested distinction between genuine strengthening and reduced applicability is resolved in favor of genuine strengthening. Integrability and rectangle conservation are conclusions about the constructed function, not premises imposed on the input data. No source state pair, repeated eigenvalue, zero speed, or positive dimension is excluded.",
      "primary_evidence": "The elaborated target universally quantifies leftState, valueAtOrigin, and rightState after the sole substantive hypothesis D001. D002 occurs within the existential conclusion. D001 requires no distinctness, nonzero eigenvalue, symmetry, or orthogonality."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "The source's unspecified representative and temporal conventions prevent identifying the entire target with the selected assertion, but do not prevent accepting a compatible, nonvacuous extension that entails it. The additional claims have concrete mathematical meaning and do not replace any source conclusion.",
      "primary_evidence": "Equation (1.11) specifies only the strict initial half-lines. The selected paragraph describes spectral solvability and forward wave propagation without asserting the target's full all-real-time, representative-level certification. D003 fixes the function appearing in every target conjunct."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "The relation directions, strictness, and exactness are correct. The integral balance has later-minus-earlier state and left-minus-right flux. Pointwise initial data and positive-time similarity are compatible additional precision. The conclusion-strength difference is recorded as strengthening rather than equivalence.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 states integral(q at t) minus integral(q at s) equals the integral from s to t of Aq(a,τ) minus Aq(b,τ). D004 preserves x<0 and x>0. D006 uses x−λt, matching equation (1.3) and the signed speeds on printed page 3."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "Finite index types merely relabel the source's finite real coordinates; the empty type adds a trivial case without removing positive dimensions. All-real-time conservation extends the initial-value assertion. Restriction of the constructed solution to t≥0 recovers the source evolution. Positive-time similarity is asserted only for this linear construction, so the source's general qualifier 'typically' is not improperly universalized.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target uses Fintype ι and Matrix ι ι Real. D002 quantifies over all real temporal endpoints, whereas the similarity conjunct requires 0<t. Printed page 5 gives initial data at t=0 and qualifies the general hyperbolic similarity description."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The arbitrary origin parameter is compatible with conservation, including stationary and repeated-speed modes. At a fixed time, changing it changes the state only at finitely many characteristic positions. At a fixed spatial endpoint, nonzero-speed modes change only at isolated crossing times. A zero-speed mode contributes zero flux because A b_p=0. Repeated speeds preserve these arguments. Positive time excludes division by zero.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003–D006 give q(x,t)=Σ_p H(c_p(L),c_p(O),c_p(R);x−λ_p t)b_p. The target supplies A b_p=λ_p b_p. The native supplement gives real interval length measure and zero singleton mass through Real.volume_Icc with equal endpoints. Equation (1.11) leaves the origin unspecified."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Existence is preserved without introducing PDE uniqueness or invertibility of A. The analytic predicate certifies the explicit finite-wave solution, rather than restricting an independently quantified class of source solutions. Its slices are finite sums of bounded step functions, hence integrable on finite intervals. Away from characteristic lines the construction is locally constant and satisfies the homogeneous PDE classically; across those lines the target supplies integral balance.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 supplies a complete eigenbasis, D068 extracts its coordinates, and D003 reconstructs the finite sum. D002 asserts spatial and temporal flux integrability and conservation. The target contains existential spectral witnesses but no uniqueness quantifier. Printed page 5 explicitly distinguishes integral conservation from classical satisfaction at discontinuities."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Resolve the reverse direction as no for the content asserted by the selected passage. Qualitative spectral solvability does not itself assert the target's particular representative for every origin value or its certification on every negative-time and crossing-time rectangle. These are additional compatible conclusions requiring construction and verification. This is not a claim that the target is mathematically false or cannot be derived using further mathematics.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed pages 5–6 defer the spectral construction to Chapter 3 and provide no characteristic-line convention. In contrast, D003 specifies the coordinatewise representative, the target quantifies every origin value, and D002 quantifies every real a,b,s,t."
    },
    {
      "item": "Disputed analytic dependencies and provenance",
      "resolution": "D065 and D089 specify genuine interval integrability and oriented vector integration. D067 selects the exact measure field of D080. The native supplement resolves D080 beyond its abbreviated inferInstance body: the measure is ordinary real length measure on the Borel space, not an arbitrary or zero measure. The declaration content establishes this interpretation; hashes alone would not.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplement explicitly expands Real.measureSpace through measureSpaceOfInnerProductSpace and states Real.volume_eq_stieltjes_id, Real.volume_Ioc, and selectedBorel. The fully explicit Real.volume_Ioc uses @MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume Real Real.measureSpace, matching D002's measure."
    },
    {
      "item": "Nonvacuity and remaining checklist consistency",
      "resolution": "The theorem has substantive moving-jump instances. For a singleton index, A=[1], L=0, and R=1, the spatial integral over [0,2] changes from 2 at time 0 to 1 at time 1, matching integrated boundary flux −1. Arbitrary origin values do not affect this calculation. The N01 status difference is terminological: there is an exact spectral construction to preserve, but no specified numerical recurrence or flux algorithm to audit.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001 admits the scalar eigenbasis; D003–D006 give the step at x=t; D002 requires integrability and the balance identity. The supplement fixes unit interval mass one. Printed page 5 presents numerical flux computation as an application of Riemann solutions, without a numerical update formula."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "For any source dimension, hyperbolic real matrix, and left/right state pair, instantiate the finite coordinate type and choose any origin value. D001 matches the source hyperbolicity condition. The target provides a complete real eigenbasis and a finite spectral construction with fronts x=λ_p t, the correct strict initial branches, positive-time dependence on x/t, and integral conservation with flux Aq under ordinary real length integration. Restricting to forward time gives the selected Riemann solution without extra source hypotheses."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "As an assertion in the selected passage, spectral solvability does not include the entire prescribed representative construction for every origin value together with slice integrability and conservation for all real temporal endpoints. Those compatible additional conclusions exceed what the passage asserts. Their independent mathematical justification does not make them explicit or implicit representative conventions of the selected source claim."
    }
  },
  "classification": "faithful-stronger",
  "accepted": true,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "genuine-conclusion-strengthening",
      "evidence": "D002–D004 and the target certify an explicit spectral representative for every origin value on all real times; printed pages 5–6 assert qualitative spectral solvability.",
      "impact": "Acceptance is as faithful-stronger, not as an exact transcription or an equivalence of arbitrary solution classes."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "evidence-verification-scope",
      "evidence": "The attached primary-source images and inline declaration dossiers, judgments, and native supplement were inspected. No tools were used.",
      "impact": "Source-byte verification, rendering hashes, native execution, and environment provenance are supplied evidence; they were not independently recomputed."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The disagreements concern additional conclusion content rather than a lost source case or an incorrect operator. Independent inspection confirms the complete real spectral hypothesis, correct coordinate reconstruction and propagation sign, strict initial branches, fixed nonzero length measure, substantive conservation, and nonvacuity. The representative convention remains harmless even for stationary characteristics because their flux vanishes. The all-real-time and representative-level certifications strengthen the selected qualitative existence assertion without restricting its applicability. No unresolved semantic item remains for this selected claim."
}
